From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wasm-dolphin patch snapshot <snapshot@local.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:33:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0074-software-raster-threads

Band-parallel software rasterizer. SWVertexLoader::DrawCurrentBatch brackets
each draw batch with Rasterizer::BeginBatch/EndBatch; triangles (and the
clipper's z-slope-only updates for culled triangles) are queued, and at
EndBatch a batch whose bounding boxes cover enough of the EFB is rasterized by
the GPU thread plus N worker threads, each claiming 24-row horizontal bands
from a shared counter and drawing every queued triangle's rows inside its band
in queue order. Small batches, and everything when no workers were requested,
are drawn inline in upstream order.

The output is byte-identical to the single-threaded rasterizer: BP/XF state is
constant within a batch (every register write flushes first), each pixel's
work touches only its own EFB pixel apart from the fastsw post-pass whose 4x4
cell never crosses a 4-row-aligned band edge, triangles stay ordered within a
band, and the zfreeze slope is updated by every triangle before the band is
applied, with the GPU thread's slope restored to the last queued triangle's
at the end of a job.

Tev accumulates its statistics and bounding-box extents per batch and
EfbInterface counts perf-query quads thread-locally; the rasterizer merges
both under one lock. Core.cpp reads the requested count from
Module.dolphinSoftwareRasterThreads (the host's ?swthreads=), publishes the
started count for GetVideoStats, and exposes a setter plus started-worker and
worker-band counters for the core's parity smoke.

